ollects every failure before it panics.\n  - `items/`: the validate parity item collection. Living specs are validated\n    with `--specs` (one item per capability), archived changes in landing order\n    against the replay before they merge, living fixtures with\n    `<stem> --type spec`, delta fixtures as `specs/alpha/spec.md` of change\n    `parity`, and targets changes against `targets/specs/`. The Rust side runs\n    `validate_living_spec`, `validate_delta`, and\n    `validate_change` + `validate_merged_change`.\n\n## Deviated\n\n- The item collection (living, delta, targets, archive) lives in\n  `openspec_parity_support/items/` rather than in the single test file. The\n  task's scope allowed only `openspec_parity_support/**` as a new path, and the\n  250-line file budget made one file awkward. The folder is documented as\n  shared, and task 3 can declare it as `pub mod openspec_parity_support;`\n  without dead-code warnings.\n- I added guards to the main test that at least one living-spec item and one\n  archived-change item were compared, so a broken enumeration fails instead of\n  passing vacuously.\n- `is_version` and `text_of` are extra CLI helpers used by the version test and\n  the no-JSON failure path.\n\n## Missing context\n\n- The scope listed only the test file and `tests/openspec_parity_support/**`,\n  so a test-local module folder such as `tests/openspec_validate_parity/` was\n  not available, which is why the item collection sits under the support\n  folder.\n\nTouched: crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_validate_parity_corpus.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/mod.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/cli.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/project.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/replay.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/report.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/trees.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/items/mod.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/items/openspec.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/items/living.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/items/delta.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/items/targets.rs, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/items/archive.rs\n---\n---\ntitle: When the validate parity test runs, the Rust validator and the OpenSpec CLI agree on every living spec, archived change and fixture except the five listed\nverify: cargo test -p osq-kernel-specs --features parity --test openspec_validate_parity_corpus -- --include-ignored\nverify_starts: red\nscope:\n  - crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml\n  - crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_validate_parity_corpus.rs\n  - crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_parity_support/**\nentry:\n  - crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml\n  - crates/kernel/specs/tests/replay_corpus.rs\n  - crates/kernel/specs/tests/golden_corpus.rs\n  - tests/openspec-differential.test.ts\nskills: []\n---\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] `crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml` gains a `[features]` table with `parity = []` and a `[[test]]` entry `name = \"openspec_validate_parity_corpus\"` with `required-features = [\"parity\"]`. Nothing else in the manifest changes, so `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` does not build the test.\n- [ ] `tests/openspec_validate_parity_corpus.rs` proves rust-specs \"Validate differences\" over every item \"OpenSpec validate parity\" lists, with the CLI found as it says. Each test carries `#[ignore = \"corpus test: runs the OpenSpec CLI on the live specs and archive\"]`. One test checks that the CLI's `--version` prints a version of the form `<n>.<n>.<n>` and fails naming the path when the CLI is missing.\n- [ ] Every item is compared before the test fails, and a failure prints each item whose results differ and each listed difference that no longer holds, with the Rust findings or merge error and OpenSpec's `ERROR` and `WARNING` messages.\n- [ ] `cargo clippy -p osq-kernel-specs --features parity --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes, and every test's doc names `Covers: rust-specs/<scenario>`.\n- [ ] `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` passes, and every existing specs test passes unchanged.\n\n## Details\n\nRun the CLI with `std::process::Command`: test targets are not runtime\ncode, so the no-runtime-Node gate does not scan them. Give each command\n`OPENSPEC_TELEMETRY=0` and the project folder as its working directory,\nand build each project under `env!(\"CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR\")`. Take the\nlanding order and the replay as `tests/replay_corpus.rs` does. Shared\nhelpers may sit in a module folder under\n`tests/openspec_parity_support/`, which task 3 reuses through `mod`.\nName items in failure output by their path relative to the repository\nor the crate.\n\nA scratch run on 2026-10-18 found the five listed differences and no\nother, over 13 living specs and 216 archived changes, in about a minute.\nIf an item differs that is not listed, first read OpenSpec's messages. If\nthe Rust validator breaks a rule as rust-specs states it, write the item\nand both results under `## Blocked`. Never edit `src/`, a fixture, an\nexisting test or anything under `openspec/`.\n\nKeep the test files under 250 lines and every function under 80. Workspace\nlints include `clippy::pedantic` and `-D warnings`. Run `cargo fmt --all`\nbefore exiting.\n\n## Scenarios\n\n- rust-specs: Validate differences\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"ls -la openspec/changes/219-rust-specs-parity/.run/results/ 2>/dev/null; echo ---; cat openspec/changes/219-rust-specs-parity/.run/results/2.md 2>/dev/null; echo ---; cat openspec/changes/219-rust-specs-parity/tasks/2.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792394594970,"end":1792394595018}}}}
