he CLI found as it says. Each test carries `#[ignore = \"corpus test: runs the OpenSpec CLI on the live specs and archive\"]`. One test checks that the CLI's `--version` prints a version of the form `<n>.<n>.<n>` and fails naming the path when the CLI is missing.\n- [ ] Every item is compared before the test fails, and a failure prints each item whose results differ and each listed difference that no longer holds, with the Rust findings or merge error and OpenSpec's `ERROR` and `WARNING` messages.\n- [ ] `cargo clippy -p osq-kernel-specs --features parity --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes, and every test's doc names `Covers: rust-specs/<scenario>`.\n- [ ] `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` passes, and every existing specs test passes unchanged.\n\n## Details\n\nRun the CLI with `std::process::Command`: test targets are not runtime\ncode, so the no-runtime-Node gate does not scan them. Give each command\n`OPENSPEC_TELEMETRY=0` and the project folder as its working directory,\nand build each project under `env!(\"CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR\")`. Take the\nlanding order and the replay as `tests/replay_corpus.rs` does. Shared\nhelpers may sit in a module folder under\n`tests/openspec_parity_support/`, which task 3 reuses through `mod`.\nName items in failure output by their path relative to the repository\nor the crate.\n\nA scratch run on 2026-10-18 found the five listed differences and no\nother, over 13 living specs and 216 archived changes, in about a minute.\nIf an item differs that is not listed, first read OpenSpec's messages. If\nthe Rust validator breaks a rule as rust-specs states it, write the item\nand both results under `## Blocked`. Never edit `src/`, a fixture, an\nexisting test or anything under `openspec/`.\n\nKeep the test files under 250 lines and every function under 80. Workspace\nlints include `clippy::pedantic` and `-D warnings`. Run `cargo fmt --all`\nbefore exiting.\n\n## Scenarios\n\n- rust-specs: Validate differences\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metada