-+{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-19T07:50:52.464Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of the work on task 3:\n\n**Deliverables**\n- `crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml`: added the second `[[test]]` entry `openspec_archive_parity_corpus` with `required-features = [\"parity\"]`.\n- `crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_archive_parity_corpus.rs` (new, 250 lines): ports `tests/openspec-differential.test.ts` against `tests/fixtures/openspec-diff/`. It builds two temp projects per case under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, runs OpenSpec `validate`/`archive`, applies each change with `merge_change`, and checks each case's `case.json` expectation (`identical`, `both-refuse`, `osq-refuses`). CLI lookup, project and tree helpers are reused through `mod openspec_parity_support`; that folder is untouched.\n\n**Verification (all green)**\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-specs --features parity --test openspec_archive_parity_corpus -- --include-ignored` → 11 passed.\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-specs --features parity --test openspec_validate_parity_corpus -- --include-ignored` → 2 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p osq-kernel-specs --features parity --all-targets -- -D warnings` → clean.\n- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` (proposal verify) → exit 0, including all corpus tests and every existing specs test.\n\n**Note (for the reviewer/planner)**: Rust cannot generate tests from a folder at runtime, so \"one test per case read from the folder\" is a per-case macro test plus a `cases_are_exactly_the_fixture_folders` test that reads the folder and asserts the set matches the declared list. This is recorded under `## Deviated` in the result file.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/219-rust-specs-parity/.run/results/3.md`."}}
