-+## Changed
-+
-+- `crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml`: added a second `[[test]]` entry,
-+  `name = "openspec_archive_parity_corpus"` with `required-features = ["parity"]`.
-+  Task 2's `[features]` table and validate-parity entry are unchanged.
-+- `crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_archive_parity_corpus.rs` (new): proves
-+  rust-specs "Archive cases match OpenSpec" over `tests/fixtures/openspec-diff/`.
-+  Each case builds two temporary projects under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, each in
-+  its own folder, from `templates/openspec` plus the case's `specs/` and
-+  `changes/`. The CLI project runs
-+  `validate <change> --type change --strict --json --no-interactive` and
-+  `archive <change> --yes --json`; the Rust project applies each change in byte
-+  order with `merge_change`, writing each text and removing an emptied
-+  capability's folder. `case.json`'s `expect` is read with `serde_json`, and the
-+  `archive --json` output with `serde_json`:
-+  - `identical`: each change validates and archives with exit 0, the two
-+    `openspec/specs/` trees are equal path for path and byte for byte, and the
-+    CLI tree is non-empty.
-+  - `both-refuse`: the first archive exits non-zero and reports
-+    `archive_spec_update_failed`; `merge_change` gives
-+    `MergeChangeError::Merge`; both trees still equal the case's `specs/`.
-+  - `osq-refuses`: `merge_change` gives `MergeChangeError::Merge` whose
-+    `MergeError` message holds `### Requirement:`; the CLI archive exits 0; no
-+    living spec it leaves holds `### Requirement: <name>` for a `TO:` name of
-+    the case's delta specs.
-+  Ten `#[ignore = "corpus test: runs the OpenSpec CLI on the differential
-+  cases"]` tests are declared, one per case, plus one that asserts the case
-+  names are exactly the fixture folders. Every test's doc names
-+  `Covers: rust-specs/archive-cases-match-openspec`. CLI lookup, project and
-+  tree helpers come from `tests/openspec_parity_support/` through `mod`; that
-+  folder is unchanged.
-+
-+## Deviated
-+
-+- "One test per case read from the folder" is implemented as a macro that
-+  declares a `#[test]` per case, plus `cases_are_exactly_the_fixture_folders`,
-+  which reads the folder and asserts the set equals the declared one. Rust
-+  cannot generate tests at run time, so a static list guarded by the exact
-+  folder check is the closest the target allows; adding or removing a case
-+  fails that test until the list is updated.
-+- The `identical` branch also asserts the CLI's archived tree is non-empty, so
-+  a scaffold or copy failure cannot pass vacuously.
-+
-+## Missing context
-+
-+- The task's "one test per case read from the folder" cannot be literal in
-+  Rust; the planner may want to say "one test per case, with a test that the
-+  case set equals the fixture folders" for future tasks.
-+
-+## Outside scope
-+
-+- None.
-+
-+Touched: crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml, crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_archive_parity_corpus.rs
