+## Changed
+
+- `crates/kernel/specs/Cargo.toml`: added a second `[[test]]` entry,
+  `name = "openspec_archive_parity_corpus"` with `required-features = ["parity"]`.
+  Task 2's `[features]` table and validate-parity entry are unchanged.
+- `crates/kernel/specs/tests/openspec_archive_parity_corpus.rs` (new): proves
+  rust-specs "Archive cases match OpenSpec" over `tests/fixtures/openspec-diff/`.
+  Each case builds two temporary projects under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, each in
+  its own folder, from `templates/openspec` plus the case's `specs/` and
+  `changes/`. The CLI project runs `validate <change> --type change --strict
+  --json --no-interactive` and `archive <change> --yes --json`; the Rust
+  project applies each change in byte order with `merge_change`, writing each
+  text and removing an emptied capability's folder. `case.json`'s `expect` and
+  the `archive --json` output are read with `serde_json`:
+  - `identical`: each change validates and archives with exit 0, the archived
+    tree is non-empty, and the two `openspec/specs/` trees are equal, path for
+    path and byte for byte.
+  - `both-refuse`: the first archive exits non-zero with a `status` entry whose
+    `code` is `archive_spec_update_failed`; `merge_change` gives
+    `MergeChangeError::Merge`; both trees still equal the case's `specs/`.
+  - `osq-refuses`: `merge_change` gives `MergeChangeError::Merge` whose
+    `MergeError` message holds `### Requirement:`; the CLI archive exits 0; no
+    living spec it leaves holds `### Requirement: <name>` for a `TO:` name of
+    the case's delta specs.
+  Eleven `#[ignore = "corpus test: runs the OpenSpec CLI on the differential
+  cases"]` tests are declared (ten cases plus the case-set check). Every test's
+  doc names `Covers: rust-specs/archive-cases-match-openspec`. CLI lookup,
+  projects and tree helpers come from `tests/openspec_parity_support/` through
+  `mod`; that folder is unchanged.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- "One test per case read from the folder" is implemented as a macro that
+  declares a `#[test]` per case, plus `cases_are_exactly_the_fixture_folders`,
+  which reads the folder and asserts the set equals the declared list. Rust
+  cannot generate tests at run time, so a static list guarded by the exact
+  folder check is the closest the target allows; adding or removing a case
+  fails that test until the list is updated. This matches the prior attempt's
+  reading of the same acceptance line.
+- The file lands at 249 lines, under the task's 250, by putting the case list
+  and the macro invocation under `#[rustfmt::skip]` so they stay on few lines.
+  No lint is loosened.
+
+## Missing context
+
+- None.
+
